    "created_at": "2026-04-20T15:22:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-20T15:22:56Z",
    "body": "The practical answer is that it should return whichever string the OS has cached so it doesn't have to perform its own IO to retrieve it. [On Linux](https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/c1f49dea2b8f335813d3b348fd39117fb8efb428/drivers/usb/core/message.c#L1000), that's the first supported language ID, with a fallback to 0x0409 (US English), and I'd assume the other platforms are similar, but doesn't seem to be documented.",
