    "created_at": "2026-04-20T23:11:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-20T23:11:47Z",
    "body": "Right, but that's an optimization and not normative behavior. And \"try to imitate what the OS does\" isn't a very principled way to design a specification. Not to mention that most OSes don't cache all the strings that WebUSB exposes, primarily the strings corresponding to non-active configurations and interface alternate settings.\n\nI also just noticed that the `serialNumber` attribute is only specified as \"SHOULD contain\" (with error handling unspecified), which _really_ doesn't feel safe for something that participates in security and permissions concerns.",
